.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Test suite for libft's singly-linked list (t_list)\&. 


.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
pulgamecanica (arosado-)
.RE
.PP
Storage convention: ft_lstnew(ptr) stores the pointer directly in \fRcontent\fP\&. Access pattern: \fR(T *)node->content\fP — wrapped here by the \fRLST_DUMMY()\fP macro\&.

.PP
Covers ft_lstnew(), ft_lstsize(), forward traversal, ft_lstdel() (pointer-and-node free), and ft_lstadd() (prepend to front)\&.

.PP
This suite is always compiled and always runs — it is not guarded by a feature flag because \fRt_list\fP is a core Libft primitive\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void test_list_suite (void )"
Run all singly-linked list assertions\&.

.PP
Builds an append-order list \fR[alpha(1) -> beta(2) -> gamma(3)]\fP, verifies ft_lstsize() and forward traversal via \fR->next\fP, then exercises ft_lstdel() (freeing all nodes with del_dummy) and asserts the head pointer is NULL afterwards\&.

.PP
A second sub-test uses ft_lstadd() (prepend) to verify that two nodes inserted as \fR[first, second]\fP are stored as \fR[second -> first]\fP in the list\&.

.PP
.RS 4
\fBPrecondition:\fP \fRLibft/srcs/ft_stdlib/\fP must be compiled and linked\&. 
.RE
.PP

